From: OpenWrt WR11000 port
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: nsscc-qca8k: keep the package bus clocks on

The QCA8084 PHY package driver only enables the package AHB/MDIO/APB/
switch-core clocks from config_init, i.e. once a MAC attaches the PHYs.
On the Cudy WR11000 the PHYs hang off a QCA8386 DSA switch whose conduit
(qcom-ppe) is a module, so the switch defers past late_initcall and
clk_disable_unused() gates these clocks first. The chip's register bus
then dies (MASK_CTRL reads back 0xbe instead of 0x17) and the switch
driver gives up with -ENODEV.

These clocks feed the register/MDIO fabric of the whole chip, nothing
works without them, and U-Boot already leaves them running. Mark them
critical.

---
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/nsscc-qca8k.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/nsscc-qca8k.c
@@ -91,7 +91,7 @@
 				&nss_cc_switch_core_clk_src.clkr.hw,
 			},
 			.num_parents = 1,
-			.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT,
+			.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT | CLK_IS_CRITICAL,
 			.ops = &clk_branch2_prepare_ops,
 		},
 	},
